# The negative variants of probe-tests/widgets/lists.probe: every test below asserts something WRONG, or crosses what the agent can do, and every one must FAIL.
# They show that the positive suite can fail, and why. This file does not end in .probe, so `probe test` never picks it up in a directory run. To run it:
#
#   cp probe-tests/negative/lists.probe.expect-fail /tmp/lists-negative.probe
#   probe test /tmp/lists-negative.probe --device <serial> -y         # (the lists build, the same probe.yaml as for lists.probe)
#
# Expected: 0 passed, 9 failed, each with the message in its comment. A test that passes is a finding: either the agent changed or the positive suite no longer proves what it says.
# Each test must fail at its own step, with the message in its comment. A failure at the `wait until` of `before each test` (a timeout
# waiting for the screen's last element) is NOT the expected failure: the screen never showed, and the run proves nothing.

before each test
  restart the app
  # Right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793): wait for the screen's last element
  # with an id (the last button of the screen).
  wait until #wf_open_tiles appears

# Expected: see "Row 150": Expected to see "text("Row 150")" but it was not found (the row is not built before the list is scrolled to it)
test "N1 a far row of a lazy list is not seen before a scroll"
  see "Row 150"

# Expected: tap "Row 150": Widget not found: text("Row 150") (a row that is not built is not scrolled to by tap)
test "N2 a far row of a lazy list is not tapped without a scroll step"
  tap "Row 150"

# Expected: scroll down until "Row 999" appears: scroll down until text("Row 999"): not found after scrolling (the list has 200 rows and the step ends with that message, it does not run on)
test "N3 scrolling to a row that does not exist ends with a failure"
  scroll down until "Row 999" appears

# Expected: see "Tapped row: 151": Expected to see "text("Tapped row: 151")" but it was not found (the tapped row is 150)
test "N4 the state names the tapped row, not the next one"
  scroll down until "Row 150" appears
  tap "Row 150"
  see "Tapped row: 151"

# Expected: see "Cell 55": Expected to see "text("Cell 55")" but it was not found (the cell is not built before the grid is scrolled to it)
test "N5 a far cell of a grid is not seen before a scroll"
  tap "Open grid"
  wait until "Cell 0" appears
  see "Cell 55"

# Expected: see "Online": Expected to see "relational("Online")" but it was not found (a subtitle is below its title, not above)
test "N6 a subtitle is not above its title"
  tap "Open tiles"
  wait until "Alice" appears
  see "Online" above "Alice"

# Expected: see "Online": Expected to see "positional("Online")" but it was not found (a title is not a container of its tile: `in "Alice"` looks inside the title's own text)
test "N7 a subtitle is not found in a tile named by its title"
  tap "Open tiles"
  wait until "Alice" appears
  see "Online" in "Alice"

# Expected: see "Long press: Alice": Expected to see "text("Long press: Alice")" but it was not found (the long press by text lands on the state text "Tapped: Alice", not on the tile)
test "N8 a long press by a name that the state text also holds"
  tap "Open tiles"
  wait until "Alice" appears
  tap "Alice"
  see "Tapped: Alice"
  long press "Alice"
  see "Long press: Alice"

# Expected: see exactly 2 "Row 0": Expected exactly 2 "text("Row 0")" but found 1 (one Text is one match: with probe_agent 0.27.0 it was counted twice, issue #800)
test "N9 one Text is not two matches"
  see exactly 2 "Row 0"
